		(uuid "5bbe65ba-2d12-4d5d-855e-bf16961d30ba")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D1:\nAD5761R (16-bit, 8 software ranges, 2.5 V 2 ppm/C reference). Range +/-5 V -> DAC_CMD +/-5 V -> +/-5 mA at G = 1, so RG3 on [6] must be DNP when the DAC drives the channel (RG3 fitted = G = 5 is for the Red Pitaya +/-1 V outputs). Alternative kept in software: range +/-3 V (RA = 100) with RG3 fitted. 1 LSB = 153 uV = 0.15 uA at G = 1 [H]. Output amp drives 2 kOhm / 1 nF [DS]; RS1 1k + D3/D4 on [6] is the load."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 60.96 0)
		(size 62 22)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d0ce1994-aec7-4139-94cc-ea515527a1f4")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D2:\nSupplies: VDD = +12V, VSS = -12V (bipolar range needs VDD 4.75-16.5 V, VSS -16.5-0 V) [DS]; DVCC = +3V3 so the logic matches the isolator side 2 and the FPGA in bypass. Decoupling drawn in the order it is laid out: rail -> 10 uF bulk -> 100 nF at the pin. VREFOUT: 10 nF to AGND per the pin table (not more: start-up time 3.5 ms [DS]). TP32 reads 2.500 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 86.36 0)
		(size 62 17)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
